  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id) not stated.\n(b_no_id_remedy) not stated.\n(c_mail_ballot_id) not stated.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship)\n(section) Sec 1, new 2-2-401(c) (citizenship portal may also use federal SAVE data, if DHS offers a secure web service)\n(quote) (c) The portal may also access data from the systematic alien verification for entitlements (SAVE) program from the United States department of homeland security, United States citizenship and immigration services (DHS-USCIS), if DHS-USCIS makes such data available via a secure web service.\n(e_other_rule) not stated.\n(other) Sec 2: effective on becoming law (Chaptered: signed 2026-04-21).\n(other) version: 3345925-Draft (2026-02-02): one operative section as above (slot d: SAVE data may be used by the portal).\n(other) version: 3426167-Chaptered (2026-04-24, Public Chapter 775, House Bill 2185 substituted for Senate Bill 2204): word-for-word the same operative text as the Draft (the Draft adds nothing the Chaptered lacks).\n(other) note: Permissive ('may also access'), not a mandate; it depends on DHS making SAVE data available by secure web service. The existing 2-2-401 portal text is not reprinted. No amendment saved or recorded at any stage, so every roll call is on the Draft text. The Calendar & Rules roll call (2026-03-16) shows only two recorded votes (0 yes, 2 no).\n(note) Off this topic: the bill sets no ID or citizenship-proof rule.",
